  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: public key pinning bypassed when no server certificate\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-80230.patch: in lib/vtls/openssl.c, treat\n       a missing server certificate as acceptable only when no pinned\n       public key is configured, so pinning is still enforced with peer\n       and host verification disabled.\n     - CVE-2026-80230\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: cookie for an exact PSL domain kept wildcard scope\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-82209.patch: in lib/cookie.c, clear the\n       tailmatch flag when a cookie's Domain attribute is itself a public\n       suffix, so it becomes host-only instead of being sent to sibling\n       subdomains.\n     - CVE-2026-82209",
